The diff contains tracked changes plus untracked filenames. Runtime files are pre-emptively untracked before this prompt; if one still appears, classify it as `delete_file`.

## Decision rules

| Path class | Action | Boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Ralph Workflow runtime artifact listed below | `delete_file` | exact basename, glob, directory, and extension rules only |
| binary, build output, cache, editor/OS file, log, coverage, backup, or temporary artifact | `delete_file`; optionally `add_to_gitignore` | delete only an actual generated file in the diff; add a pattern only when project-wide or recurrent |
| machine-local file or pattern | `add_to_git_exclude` | use for the recognized secret family below and editor state |
| generated untracked text/JSON named for session, transcript, prompt, analysis, checkpoint, verify, output, report, log, trace, debug, dump, temp, artifact, capture, completion, note, pipeline, response, review, summary, worker, chat, message, plan, model, llm, brainstorm, interaction, or inference | `delete_file` | untracked only |
| generated untracked source whose name contains `temp`, `tmp`, `scratch`, `generated`, `throwaway`, or `dump`, or lies under `tmp/`, `temp/`, `generated/`, or `artifacts/` | `delete_file` | untracked only |
| uncertain, user-authored, intentional config, test, documentation, lockfile, or tracked source | no action | never change commit meaning |

Recognized secrets are `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `secrets.yml`, and `credentials.json`. `add_to_git_exclude` preserves their working-tree copies and untracks only this recognized family; it never untracks arbitrary project files.

Common generated categories include compiled extensions (`.exe`, `.dll`, `.so`, `.dylib`, `.pdb`, `.a`, `.o`, `.class`, `.pyc`, `.pyo`); build/dependency/cache directories (`build/`, `dist/`, `node_modules/`, `vendor/`, `.next/`, `.nuxt/`, `.output/`, `__pycache__/`, `.eggs/`, `*.egg-info/`, `.bundle/`, `.gradle/`, `.m2/`); editor/OS files (`.DS_Store`, `Thumbs.db`, `._*`, `*.swp`, `*.swo`, `*.orig`, `*~`, `.vscode/`, `.idea/`); temporary/log/coverage files (`*.bak`, `*.tmp`, `*.temp`, `*.old`, `*.rej`, `*.patch`, `*.log`, `*.trace`, `*.profile`, `coverage/`, `.coverage`, `coverage.xml`, `htmlcov/`, `.pytest_cache/`, `.mypy_cache/`, `.ruff_cache/`).

Never remove dependency lockfiles such as `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock`, `Cargo.lock`, `poetry.lock`, `uv.lock`, `Pipfile.lock`, `composer.lock`, `Gemfile.lock`, or `go.sum`.

## Ralph Workflow runtime artifact allowlist

`delete_file` is allowed for:

- `.agent/` top-level basenames: `PRODUCT_CRITERIA.md`, `PLAN.md`, `ISSUES.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_RESULT.md`, `FIX_RESULT.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_ANALYSIS_DECISION.md`, `PLANNING_ANALYSIS_DECISION.md`, `REVIEW_ANALYSIS_DECISION.md`, `checkpoint.json`, `rebase_checkpoint.json`, `rebase_checkpoint.json.bak`, `auto_integrate_in_progress.json`, `rebase.lock`, `start_commit`, `mcp.toml`, `state.db`, `state.db-wal`, `state.db-shm`.
- `.agent/completion_seen_*.json` and root `checkpoint.json`.
- `.agent/raw/*.log`.
- `.agent/tmp/*.{log,md,json}`.
- `.agent/artifacts/*.md`.
- `.agent/receipts/<run-id>/*.json`.
- `.agent/prompt_history/*.json`.
- `.agent/artifact-formats/*.md`.
- `.agent/workers/<unit>/**/*.{log,md,json}`.

These directory rules are extension-restricted. Any other extension is user-authored: for example `.agent/raw/script.py`, `.agent/tmp/config.yaml`, `.agent/artifacts/notes.json`, `.agent/receipts/run-1/note.md`, `.agent/artifact-formats/data.json`, or worker source files. Top-level `.agent/` files absent from the basename list and arbitrary `.agent/` subdirectories are also user-authored. Never recommend broad deletion of `.agent/`, `artifacts/`, or `reports/`.

If an unsafe `delete_file` action is rejected, use the returned retry hint to omit it or reclassify a genuinely machine-local path as `add_to_git_exclude`. When unsure, submit no action.

